theorem sum-formula
  metamath    arisum
  let n ∈ ℕ                                                           (H1)
  then Σ(k = 1 to n) k = n(n + 1)/2

define S(m) := Σ(j = 1 to m) j, for m ∈ ℕ                             (D1)
       reads the sum of the first m natural numbers

1.  S(n) = n(n + 1)/2
    induction on n starting at 1, from H1

    base
    1.1.  Σ(j = 1 to 1) j = 1
          thm:stdlib/sums/sum-single a := 1
          requires 1 ∈ ℤ: arithmetic

    1.2.  S(1) = 1(1 + 1)/2
          calculation
            S(1) = Σ(j = 1 to 1) j       D1
                 = 1                     1.1
                 = 1(1 + 1)/2            arithmetic

    step
    1.3.  For every k ∈ ℕ, if S(k) = k(k + 1)/2
          then S(k + 1) = (k + 1)((k + 1) + 1)/2.
          fix
          let k ∈ ℕ                                                   (K)
          assume S(k) = k(k + 1)/2                                    (IH)

          1.3.1.  Σ(j = 1 to k + 1) j = Σ(j = 1 to k) j + (k + 1)
                  thm:stdlib/sums/sum-extended a := 1, n := k
                  requires 1 ∈ ℤ: arithmetic
                  requires k ∈ ℤ: thm:stdlib/numbers/nat-int, from K
                  requires k ≥ 1: thm:stdlib/numbers/nat-ge-1, from K

          1.3.2.  S(k + 1) = S(k) + (k + 1)
                  calculation
                    S(k + 1) = Σ(j = 1 to k + 1) j          D1
                             = Σ(j = 1 to k) j + (k + 1)    1.3.1
                             = S(k) + (k + 1)               D1
                  requires k + 1 ∈ ℕ: thm:stdlib/numbers/nat-closure a := k, b := 1, from K
                  requires 1 ∈ ℕ: arithmetic
                  requires k ∈ ℕ: from K

          1.3.3.  S(k) + (k + 1) = k(k + 1)/2 + (k + 1)
                  substitute S(k) = k(k + 1)/2 (IH)

          1.3.4.  k(k + 1)/2 + (k + 1) = (k + 1)((k + 1) + 1)/2
                  algebra
                  requires 2 ≠ 0: arithmetic
                  requires k ∈ ℝ: thm:stdlib/numbers/nat-real, from K

          1.3.5.  S(k + 1) = (k + 1)((k + 1) + 1)/2
                  calculation
                    S(k + 1) = S(k) + (k + 1)               1.3.2
                             = k(k + 1)/2 + (k + 1)         1.3.3
                             = (k + 1)((k + 1) + 1)/2       1.3.4

2.  Σ(k = 1 to n) k = n(n + 1)/2
    calculation
      Σ(k = 1 to n) k = S(n)              D1
                      = n(n + 1)/2        1
    requires n ∈ ℕ: from H1
